  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rakesh Ratanlal Pareek vs The State Of Maharashtra on 26 August, 2022 Author: Anuja Prabhudessai Bench: Anuja Prabhudessai 8 aba 2736-21+5.d In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2736 Of 2021 Shivaji Bayaji Vhanmane & Anr. ..Applicants v/s. The State of Maharashtra . ..Respondents With Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2740 Of 2021 Sanjay Nivrutti Javir ..Applicant v/s. The State of Maharashtra . ..Respondents With Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2738 Of 2021 Ranjit Shivaji Vhanmane ..Applicant v/s. The State of Maharashtra . ..Respondents With Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2755 Of 2021 Yuvraj Bhagvan Aldar & Anr. ..Applicants v/s. The State of Maharashtra . ..Respondents With Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2810 Of 2021 Rakesh Ratanlal Pareek vs The State Of Maharashtra on 26 August, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/184864453/ 1 Digitally signed by Prasanna P Prasanna P Salgaonkar Salgaonkar Date: 2022.08.29 13:06:21 +0530 pps 1 of 8 aba 2736-21+5.doc Rakesh Ratanlal Pareek ..Applicant v/s. The State of Maharashtra . ..Respondents Mr. Umesh Mankapure for the Applicant in Aba/2736/2021, Aba/ 2738/2021, Aba/2740/2021 and Aba/2755/2021. Mr. Ajit Savagave for the Applicant in Aba/2810/2021 Mrs. G.P.Mulekar, App for the State. Police Naik Mr. Awatade, from Sangola Police Stn. Coram : Anuja Prabhudessai, J. Dated : 26th August, 2022. P.C. 1. These applications under Section 438 of Cr.P.C. are filed by the aforesaid Applicants apprehending their arrest in Crime No. 1232 of 2021 registered with Sangola Police Station, Solapur, for the offences under Section 272, 273, 420, 328 r/w. 34 of Indian Penal Code, Section 26(1), 26(2), 26(2)(v), 27(3)(e), 30(2)(a), 38(6) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006. 2. The aforesaid crime was registered pursuant to the FIR lodged by the Food and Drugs Inspector.",
    "facts": "These applications under Section 438 of Cr.P.C. are filed by the aforesaid Applicants apprehending their arrest in Crime No. 1232 of 2021 registered with Sangola Police Station, Solapur, for the offences under Section 272, 273, 420, 328 r/w. 34 of Indian Penal Code, Section 26(1), 26(2), 26(2)(v), 27(3)(e), 30(2)(a), 38(6) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006. 2. The aforesaid crime was registered pursuant to the FIR lodged by the Food and Drugs Inspector. The case of the prosecution is that the shop by name Vithai Milk and Food Products was raided. The Applicants in BA/2736/2021, BA/2738/2021, BA/2740/2021 and BA/2755/2021 are the partners of the said shop. It is alleged pps 2 of 4 8 aba 2736-21+5.doc that these Applicants were found adulterating cow milk and Buffalo milk. Whereas, the Applicant in ABA/2810/2021 has allegedly sold Whey powder of Amul brand to the partners of the said shop. The articles used for adulteration were seized. 3. The Applicants were granted pre-arrest bail on 8.11.2021. It is stated that the Applicants have reported to the Investigating Officer. They have been interrogated and upon completion of investigation chargesheet has been filed. Presence of the Applicants is no longer required for the purpose of interrogation.",
